From 9f0f91c030173c99f5064490074e6e0f69803d20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 00:11:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/19] camera: port OP15 private-space + Gallery/FileManager
 framework support

Port the OP15InfinityX private-space / Gallery / FileManager framework
support into the vendor/oplus/camera extraction and policy root (kept
here rather than a device/oneplus/infiniti-camera tree):

- apk fixup framework (apk_fixups_op15.py, apk_fixups_camera_op15.py,
  apk_fixups_gallery_op15.py) driven from extract-files.py: anchor-based,
  apktool-verified manifest/smali edits for OplusCamera (component-safe
  alias + OEM-perm strip), OppoGallery2 (set-as-wallpaper ATTACH_DATA
  intent) and the cryptoeng framework payload (permissions XML +
  manifest).
- the OEM cryptoeng App-Lock HAL payload (blobs, framework, permissions
  and vendor sepolicy: hal_cryptoeng_oplus / hwservice / service / tee /
  file types and contexts) plus libqsee_keybox_ca.so so the odm cryptoeng
  service links.
- privileged-permission allowlist and hidden-api exemptions for the
  shipped OPLUS apps and the OPPO component-safe / private-safe gates.

None of the seven OP15InfinityX OEM security / private-space apps is
shipped:

- the three system_ext priv-apps (com.oplus.pantanal.ums,
  com.oplus.phonemanager, com.oplus.exsystemservice): with
  ro.control_privapp_permissions=enforce they request platform privileged
  permissions with no allowlist entry and turn systemReady into a
  system_server bootloop. None is load-bearing for the camera stack
  (their absence is tolerated via caught NameNotFound / missing-provider
  paths).
- the four security / private-space siblings, per the maximal-de-bloat
  decision:
  - com.oplus.safecenter (SafeCenter / Security Centre): crashed on
    camera launch (NoSuchMethodError in its own SecureSafeApp.onCreate
    against the oplus-fwk stub). The camera's only touch point,
    GalleryHelper's query of content://com.oplus.provider.SafeProvider
    (limit_use_app check), is null-checked and wrapped in try/catch, so
    the provider's absence fails closed.
  - com.oplus.encryption (FileEncryption): the Private Safe vault;
    Gallery/FileManager "move to Private Safe" flows degrade benignly.
  - com.oneplus.filemanager (FileManager): functional duplicate of the
    LOS file manager.
  - com.oplus.securitypermission (SecurityPermission): dropping its
    permission-definer fixup un-defines the com.oplus.permission.safe.*
    signature family -> OEM cross-app guards become deny-all to external
    callers, benign; its two real perms (SECURITY_ACTION,
    safe.SMS.BROADCAST) have no shipped consumer.

The cryptoeng App-Lock HAL is kept (shared by the FIDO/cryptoeng
device-attestation path) and so is libOplusSecurity.so (a base camera
blob from the initial port). See docs/PRIVATE_SPACE.md for the
disposition and future-work note.

Original OP15InfinityX port + Gallery/FileManager fixups by Jonas Salo
<salomannen1234@gmail.com>; OEM security / private-space apps dropped and
reconciled for the infiniti-camera-port build.

